From e33d4f520c20cf3002183ad0bd1d31df61f226a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:42:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Input: rmi4 - complete suspend after powering down I2C
 transport

rmi_i2c_suspend() disables the transport supplies even when suspending the
RMI functions failed. Returning that error makes the PM core abort system
suspend without marking this device suspended. Its resume callback is
therefore skipped and the touchscreen remains powered down.

Report the failed sleep command and complete the callback successfully,
as rmi_i2c_runtime_suspend() already does. This lets the PM core restore
the supplies and resume the RMI functions on either normal resume or
unwind after another device fails. Correct the copied resume diagnostic
at the same time.

The downstream LG Fx0 encountered a sleep-command timeout when display
shutdown made its in-cell controller unavailable. Adapt the existing
downstream fix by Timothy Schmidt without requiring its separate reset
GPIO or panel-follower additions.

This draft was prepared with an AI coding assistant. Human review and
DCO certification remain pending.

Fixes: 946c8432aab0 ("Input: synaptics-rmi4 - support regulator supplies")
---
 drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
index b0b36ddb2760..58009c0c1cea 100644
--- a/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/rmi4/rmi_i2c.c
@@ -294,12 +294,16 @@ static int rmi_i2c_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	ret = rmi_driver_suspend(rmi_i2c->xport.rmi_dev, true);
 	if (ret)
-		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to resume device: %d\n", ret);
+		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to suspend device: %d\n", ret);
 
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(rmi_i2c->supplies),
 			       rmi_i2c->supplies);
 
-	return ret;
+	/*
+	 * The transport is powered down even if the sleep command failed.
+	 * Complete suspend so the PM core will call our resume callback.
+	 */
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int rmi_i2c_resume(struct device *dev)
